phase P4
title Persistence and complete evidence

tasks
    T401
        title        PersistenceProviderAndStorage
        status       open
        priority     high
        blocked_by   [
                     @task.Rewrite.T105,
                     @task.Rewrite.T107,
                     @task.Rewrite.T201
                     ]
        derives_from [
                     @plan.PersistenceV2.O1,
                     @plan.PersistenceV2.V1,
                     @plan.PersistenceV2.D1,
                     @plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.O2,
                     @plan.ProjectDelivery.O3,
                     @plan.DiagnosticsContract.O3
                     ]
        satisfies    [@plan.PersistenceV2.O1, @plan.DiagnosticsContract.O3]
        description
            Deliver typed optional provider declarations and storage boundary without 
            construction-time I/O. Ordered work: (1) define exact provider/codec types and default 
            persist=false behavior; (2) keep construction inert; (3) validate detached payloads 
            before installation; (4) prove provider read/write error mapping and optional 
            capability behavior. Permitted paths: persistence/provider.ts and 
            persistence/test/provider-types.test.ts, provider.test.ts. Shared-write boundary: T107 
            owns structural codec core and initial evidence record contract; T409 owns bounded 
            envelope integration. Do not add storage I/O during Runtime construction. Evidence: 
            provider-types.test.ts and provider.test.ts.
        acceptance
            Positive: optional provider surface preserves exact data and failure types, omitted 
            persistence stays disabled, and construction performs no read/write. Check: 
            persistence/test/provider-types.test.ts and provider.test.ts; expected: exact types 
            compile and provider counters remain zero before ready.

            Failure: malformed provider data, codec failure, or provider read/write error maps to a 
            typed diagnostic before installing a candidate record. Check: 
            persistence/test/provider.test.ts; expected: existing committed state remains unchanged.

    T402
        title        DurableSelectionAndDetachedBoot
        status       open
        priority     high
        blocked_by   [
                     @T401,
                     @task.Rewrite.T201,
                     @task.Rewrite.T202,
                     @task.Rewrite.T204,
                     @task.Rewrite.T303
                     ]
        derives_from [
                     @plan.PersistenceV2.O2,
                     @plan.PersistenceV2.V2,
                     @plan.ApplicationsAndActors.O3,
                     @plan.ApplicationsAndActors.O4,
                     @plan.ProjectDelivery.O3
                     ]
        satisfies    [@plan.PersistenceV2.O2, @plan.ApplicationsAndActors.O3]
        description
            Deliver durable selection and persistence-backed readiness/boot through the production 
            Runtime, preserving detached validation before service acquisition, installation, 
            activation, or handle escape. Ordered work: (1) consume provider and no-persistence 
            readiness seams; (2) select the compatible durable record; (3) validate candidate 
            record and App identity detached; (4) acquire requirements and install/activate only 
            after validation; (5) prove base-readiness and persisted-readiness outcomes. Permitted 
            paths: persistence/bootstrap.ts, persistence/test/bootstrap.test.ts, and the production 
            Runtime ready assembly owner. Shared-write boundary: T201/T202 remain base increments; 
            this task owns the persistence boot increment. Evidence: bootstrap.test.ts.
        acceptance
            Positive: a valid compatible persisted record is selected, validated detached, then 
            installed before actors/handle become available. Check: 
            persistence/test/bootstrap.test.ts; expected: ready exposes the restored runtime only 
            after all validation and acquisition succeed.

            Failure: missing/incompatible/corrupt record or acquisition failure rejects readiness 
            before activation and handle escape. Check: persistence/test/bootstrap.test.ts; 
            expected: prior durable and in-memory state remain intact and no actor starts.

    T403
        title        ContextClosedCapture
        status       open
        priority     medium
        blocked_by   [@T401, @T402, @task.Rewrite.T313, @task.Rewrite.T204]
        derives_from [
                     @plan.PersistenceV2.O3,
                     @plan.PersistenceV2.V3,
                     @plan.ApplicationsAndActors.O6,
                     @plan.ApplicationsAndActors.O7,
                     @plan.ProjectDelivery.O3
                     ]
        satisfies    [@plan.PersistenceV2.O3]
        description
            Deliver one consistent capture cut across actor, resource/store, operation, context, 
            and evidence state. Ordered work: (1) use the integrated P3 publication owner; (2) 
            capture only values belonging to the committed cut; (3) include the exact context 
            closure required by T204’s settled provider bindings; (4) prove capture racing commit 
            yields a coherent old or new cut. Permitted paths: persistence/capture.ts and 
            persistence/test/capture.test.ts. Shared-write boundary: this is a capture reader, not 
            a second actor/store publication owner. Selector-defect policy T206/T205 does not gate 
            settled closure capture: suspended or incomplete context debt is rejected. Independent 
            provider/boot/schema tasks proceed. Evidence: capture.test.ts.
        acceptance
            Positive: direct and transitive eligible providers are captured with exact consumer 
            ref, provider ref, binding path, and observed revisions. Check: 
            persistence/test/capture.test.ts; expected: one complete pre-publication or 
            post-publication cut, with no mixed store revision.

            Failure: opaque, persist:false, filter-excluded, missing, disposed, or otherwise 
            invalid providers anywhere in direct/transitive closure reject the whole selection with 
            NonDurableContextProvider. Concurrent closure/store/revision mismatch and suspended 
            context debt return retryable ConcurrentCapture. With multiple invalid bindings, 
            diagnostics retain each durable consumer ID, opaque provider diagnostic ID, provider 
            machine ID, and every failing contextBindings.<key> path; remediation names 
            actorRef(providerMachine,id) and runtime.ensureActor(ref,...). Check: 
            persistence/test/capture.test.ts; expected: exact canonical code/details and no partial 
            record, durable write, Runtime mutation, promotion, substitution, rebinding, or 
            omission.

            No-work: capture invokes no adapter, emits no context event, and changes no Runtime 
            truth. Selector-defect behavior remains local to T205 and is not a prerequisite for 
            this settled capture proof. Check: persistence/test/capture.test.ts; expected: 
            adapter/event counters remain zero.

    T404
        title        HydrationWithoutReplay
        status       open
        priority     high
        blocked_by   [
                     @T401,
                     @T402,
                     @task.Rewrite.T303,
                     @task.Rewrite.T309,
                     @task.Rewrite.T310,
                     @T410
                     ]
        derives_from [
                     @plan.PersistenceV2.O4,
                     @plan.PersistenceV2.V4,
                     @plan.Transactions.O4,
                     @plan.Transactions.V4,
                     @plan.ProjectDelivery.O3
                     ]
        satisfies    [@plan.PersistenceV2.O4, @plan.Transactions.O4]
        description
            Deliver resource/transaction hydration that normalizes ownership and lifecycle state 
            without invoking lookup, transaction, or stream work. Ordered work: (1) restore 
            committed resource facts and generations; (2) normalize local interrupted operations; 
            (3) preserve remote unknown/reconcile-required truth unless persisted evidence proves 
            the invocation had not begun; (4) install hydrated facts after detached validation and 
            the canonical schema owner T410. Permitted paths: persistence/hydration.ts and 
            persistence/test/hydration.test.ts plus operation remote status facts consumed through 
            T310. Shared-write boundary: stream projection hydration is split into T414 and 
            excluded here, allowing settled resource/transaction restore to proceed independently 
            of capture races and Streams.Q1. Evidence: hydration.test.ts.
        acceptance
            Positive: resource values/generations restore and local pending work becomes 
            interrupted; remote pending work becomes unknown/reconcile-required unless evidence 
            establishes no invocation. Check: persistence/test/hydration.test.ts; expected: 
            restored facts preserve exact operation truth.

            Failure: hydration never replays lookup, mutation, or remote work; invalid state and 
            counter exhaustion reject before installation. Check: 
            persistence/test/hydration.test.ts; expected: invocation counters remain zero and prior 
            committed state remains.

    T405
        title        OrderedWritesAndLastGoodRecord
        status       open
        priority     high
        blocked_by   [@T401, @T402, @T403, @task.Rewrite.T203, @T409, @T410]
        derives_from [
                     @plan.PersistenceV2.O5,
                     @plan.PersistenceV2.V5,
                     @plan.PersistenceV2.D2,
                     @plan.ProjectDelivery.O3
                     ]
        satisfies    [@plan.PersistenceV2.O5]
        description
            Deliver Runtime-owned persistence writes ordered by committed sequence with exact 
            lifecycle/disposal behavior and last-good-record retention. Ordered work: (1) observe 
            only committed cuts; (2) consume bounded envelope/canonical schema owners T409/T410 and 
            serialize writes in cut order; (3) preserve last good record on write/encoding failure; 
            (4) flush only the accepted prefix during disposal. Permitted paths: 
            persistence/writes.ts and persistence/test/writes.test.ts. Shared-write boundary: use 
            T403 capture output and T401 provider; do not add an independent publisher or retention 
            policy. Evidence: writes.test.ts.
        acceptance
            Positive: multiple accepted captures persist in commit order and disposal flushes 
            through the accepted terminal prefix. Check: persistence/test/writes.test.ts; expected: 
            provider records are ordered and flush completion matches the accepted prefix.

            Failure: failed write or encoding leaves the last good record readable and does not 
            reorder later accepted writes. Check: persistence/test/writes.test.ts; expected: 
            durable bytes remain the last successful record and failure is surfaced.

    T406
        title        SettledInspectionProjections
        status       open
        priority     medium
        blocked_by   [
                     @task.Rewrite.T102,
                     @task.Rewrite.T210,
                     @task.Rewrite.T313
                     ]
        derives_from [
                     @plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.O1,
                     @plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.V1,
                     @plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.C1
                     ]
        satisfies    [@plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.O1]
        description
            Deliver settled pure inspection projections over declarations and committed production 
            snapshots, excluding unresolved Q2 call forms. Ordered work: (1) consume exact settled 
            model/snapshot inputs; (2) derive present declarations and committed facts without 
            starting work or inventing history; (3) keep private wire types out of public routes; 
            (4) prove projections are defensive and consistent. Permitted paths: 
            inspect/projections.ts, inspect/test/projections.test.ts, and public declarations only 
            for settled routes. Shared-write boundary: T407 owns final call forms; T408 owns 
            evidence sinks and T409/T410 artifact encoding. Evidence: 
            inspect/test/projections.test.ts plus focused type/privacy checks.
        acceptance
            Positive: settled projections are pure, return only declaration-derived or committed 
            facts, and have one formatter/owner for each projection. Check: 
            inspect/test/projections.test.ts and check:types; expected: no I/O, scheduling, or 
            actual-completion claim occurs.

            Failure: fabricated/mutable lookalikes and unsupported call forms are rejected; private 
            trace/schema types do not appear in packed public declarations. Check: projection 
            tests, check:types, and packed-consumer declarations; expected: inputs are defensively 
            validated and private types remain absent.

    T407
        title        InspectionCallForms
        status       draft
        priority     medium
        blocked_by   [@T406, @T409, @T410, @T412, @T416]
        derives_from [
                     @plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.O1,
                     @plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.O6,
                     @plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.V1,
                     @plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.V6,
                     @plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.Q2
                     ]
        satisfies    [@plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.O1, @plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.O6]
        description
            After InspectionAndArtifacts.Q2 is decided, add only the approved remaining inspection 
            and artifact call forms: activity/behavior analysis, compression/decompression, trace 
            analysis, behavior slicing/diff rendering. Ordered work: (1) define exact accepted 
            public arguments/results; (2) keep the established diagnostic mapping and inert/pure 
            behavior; (3) add positive and negative API/runtime vectors. Permitted paths: public 
            inspection entrypoint, inspect owner, artifact API, and focused inspect/artifact tests. 
            Shared-write boundary: settled projections, codec core, bounded sinks, and private 
            schema implementation proceed independently. This task remains draft and cannot infer 
            Q2 from retained declarations. The local InspectionAndArtifacts.Q2 decision Task is 
            T416; only its approved forms are implemented here.
        acceptance
            Positive: each explicitly approved Q2 call form has exact types and follows its settled 
            pure/query behavior. Check: inspect/artifact type and behavior tests; expected: only 
            approved arguments/results compile and query results preserve incomplete-evidence 
            meaning.

            Failure: unsupported arguments, compressed shares, malformed selectors, or unavailable 
            evidence reject through canonical diagnostics without runtime/gateway work. Check: 
            focused inspect/artifact tests; expected: exact diagnostic path/reason and no execution 
            side effect.

    T408
        title        BoundedEvidenceSinks
        status       open
        priority     high
        blocked_by   [
                     @task.Rewrite.T107,
                     @task.Rewrite.T210,
                     @task.Rewrite.T313
                     ]
        derives_from [
                     @plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.O3,
                     @plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.V3,
                     @plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.D3,
                     @plan.ProjectDelivery.O3
                     ]
        satisfies    [@plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.O3]
        description
            Deliver bounded evidence sink ownership, ordering, truncation, drain/dispose, and 
            failure isolation for records accepted at the production commit boundary. Ordered work: 
            (1) consume P1 T107 evidence record contract and P2/T313 committed sequence; (2) 
            implement bounded retained evidence and sink lifecycle; (3) prove stalled/failing sinks 
            do not block commit acknowledgment or healthy sinks; (4) prove exhaustion/capacity 
            refusal occurs before commit. Permitted paths: runtime-next evidence sink owner and 
            runtime-next/test/evidence-sink-owner.test.ts. Shared-write boundary: T313 owns 
            producer acceptance; T408 owns sink retention/attachment, not actor mutation or durable 
            history. Evidence: evidence-sink-owner.test.ts.
        acceptance
            Positive: ordered accepted evidence is bounded, markers identify greatest omitted 
            sequence, clear preserves monotonic sequence, and drain/dispose waits only for its 
            accepted prefix. Check: runtime-next/test/evidence-sink-owner.test.ts; expected: 
            retained tail and markers exactly match configured capacity.

            Failure: a stalled sink cannot block acknowledgment/StoreFanout; failure detaches only 
            that sink; capacity or sequence exhaustion refuses before actor/store commit. Check: 
            evidence-sink-owner.test.ts; expected: healthy sinks continue and no partial commit 
            occurs.

    T409
        title        BoundedEnvelopeIntegration
        status       open
        priority     high
        blocked_by   [@task.Rewrite.T107, @T401]
        derives_from [
                     @plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.O2,
                     @plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.V2,
                     @plan.PersistenceV2.O1,
                     @plan.PersistenceV2.V1,
                     @plan.ProjectDelivery.O2,
                     @plan.ProjectDelivery.O3
                     ]
        satisfies    [@plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.O2, @plan.PersistenceV2.O1]
        description
            Integrate the persistence/artifact envelope encoders and decoders with P1 T107's shared 
            structural walker and UTF-8 policy, preserving exact bounds and diagnostics. This task 
            does not create or fork the codec core. Ordered work: (1) consume the shared portable 
            structural codec; (2) define closed persistence/artifact envelope use sites and byte 
            boundaries; (3) validate malformed/oversized input before Runtime installation or 
            mutation; (4) prove host-neutral byte behavior at the envelope boundary. Permitted 
            paths: artifact/envelope.ts, persistence envelope adapters, artifact tests under 
            src/artifact/tests, and persistence provider tests. Shared-write boundary: T107 alone 
            owns structural traversal/UTF-8 core; T410 owns canonical schema. Evidence: artifact 
            envelope and persistence provider tests.
        acceptance
            Positive: persistence and artifact envelopes use one shared codec core, enforce exact 
            structural/byte bounds, and produce equal portable bytes for equal accepted inputs. 
            Check: artifact envelope tests and persistence provider tests; expected: no duplicate 
            traversal policy and deterministic bytes.

            Failure: malformed JSON, duplicate keys where detectable, cycles, negative zero, 
            non-finite values, invalid UTF-8, trailing/concatenated compressed data, and over-bound 
            input reject before installation or mutation with owning diagnostics. Check: artifact 
            codec tests; expected: decompression stops at the output bound and invalid candidates 
            leave current state unchanged.

    T410
        title        CanonicalWireSchemas
        status       open
        priority     high
        blocked_by   [@T409, @T413]
        derives_from [
                     @plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.O4,
                     @plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.V4,
                     @plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.C1,
                     @plan.PersistenceV2.O1,
                     @plan.PersistenceV2.O2
                     ]
        satisfies    [@plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.O4]
        description
            Implement the closed private persistence/artifact schemas specified by T413, preserving 
            explicit normative fields, correlation and identity laws, canonical ordering, 
            diagnostics, and shared bounds. Ordered work: (1) consume the approved private schema 
            Spec; (2) implement one production decoder/encoder owner per envelope; (3) validate 
            exact positive/negative vectors before acquisition; (4) keep private types unexported. 
            Permitted paths: artifact schema/codec modules and 
            packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/artifact/tests; persistence envelope adapters only 
            where the schema requires them. Shared-write boundary: T413 owns representation design; 
            T409 owns shared bound/codec integration; no new public schema or alternate decoder. 
            Evidence: artifact schema tests, check:types, packed-consumer checks.
        acceptance
            Positive: valid persistence/raw behavior/trace values round-trip to exact decoded model 
            and canonical bytes, with authored order and fingerprints preserved. Check: artifact 
            schema tests; expected: exact byte/model parity and private schemas remain 
            package-private.

            Failure: unknown members, invalid discriminator/version/identity, field-correlation 
            errors, malformed fingerprints, and wrong receiving App reject before Runtime/service 
            acquisition with exact canonical diagnostics. Check: artifact schema tests and packed 
            consumers; expected: no partial install and no private schema export.

    T411
        title        DefensiveRedactedShares
        status       open
        priority     medium
        blocked_by   [@T409, @T410]
        derives_from [
                     @plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.O5,
                     @plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.V5,
                     @plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.D2
                     ]
        satisfies    [@plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.O5]
        description
            Deliver deterministic defensive share export using the canonical raw artifact model 
            while keeping share input distinct from evidence authority. Ordered work: (1) consume 
            canonical wire models from T410; (2) validate redaction paths/order/replacements and 
            protected fields; (3) export deterministic uncompressed share bytes; (4) prove inputs, 
            bytes, and Runtime/persistence truth remain isolated. Permitted paths: 
            artifact/share.ts and artifact share tests. Shared-write boundary: no share decoder is 
            an evidence importer; no raw records, Runtime, or persistence state may be rewritten. 
            Evidence: share export tests.
        acceptance
            Positive: default export is byte-identical to raw canonical export; explicit redactions 
            are deterministic and reduce only permitted values. Check: artifact share tests; 
            expected: caller mutation after export does not change returned bytes or source data.

            Failure: malformed, duplicate, overlapping, wildcard, structural, missing, 
            out-of-range, or protected-field paths reject with exact diagnostic precedence; share 
            bytes fail raw import as WrongArtifactKind before identity checks. Check: artifact 
            share tests; expected: raw evidence, Runtime, and persistence remain byte-identical.

    T412
        title        TraceSummaryAndComparison
        status       open
        priority     medium
        blocked_by   [@T408, @T410]
        derives_from [
                     @plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.O6,
                     @plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.V6,
                     @plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.C2
                     ]
        satisfies    [@plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.O6]
        description
            Deliver settled trace summary, complete-only proof/equality, ordered behavior 
            comparison, and incomplete-evidence diagnostics using canonical records. Ordered work: 
            (1) consume evidence from T408 and canonical models from T410; (2) preserve exact 
            selector parsing and diagnostic meanings for settled forms; (3) compare the same 
            ordered behavior projection; (4) prove truncated inputs cannot yield complete 
            proof/equality. Permitted paths: artifact/trace-analysis.ts and artifact comparison 
            tests. Shared-write boundary: unresolved final call names/argument/result forms remain 
            T407/Q2; do not add unapproved routes. Evidence: trace and comparison tests.
        acceptance
            Positive: behavior diff and live behavior check compare the same ordered canonical 
            behavior projection, optionally scoped by module; complete equal/different artifacts 
            compare against that projection; matching facts under truncation yield incomplete and 
            differing retained facts yield different; summary includes the truncation marker. 
            Check: artifact comparison tests; expected: exact outcome and section order.

            Failure: incomplete proof and unknown selector reject with 
            Failure/InvalidArtifactOperand and exact marker/path/reason, incompatible identity is 
            failure rather than difference. Check: trace analysis tests; expected: no gateway or 
            Runtime execution and no incomplete proof succeeds.

            Behavior failure: incompatible app/fingerprint or malformed selector returns the owning 
            Failure diagnostic; incomplete trace never yields proof/equality. Check: trace analysis 
            and behavior comparison tests; expected: exact marker/path/reason, no gateway/Runtime 
            execution, and no incomplete proof succeeds.

    T413
        title        SpecifyPrivateArtifactWireModel
        status       open
        priority     high
        blocked_by   [
                     @task.Rewrite.T107,
                     @task.Rewrite.T301,
                     @task.Rewrite.T306,
                     @task.Rewrite.T310,
                     @task.Rewrite.T311,
                     @task.Rewrite.T313,
                     @T408
                     ]
        derives_from [
                     @plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.O4,
                     @plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.V4,
                     @plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.C1,
                     @plan.ProjectDelivery.O4
                     ]
        satisfies    [@plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.O4]
        description
            Author a concrete module Spec for the private nested persistence/artifact wire 
            representation before schema implementation. Deliverable: 
            specs/artifact/ArtifactWire.spec, owned by this task, defining one closed production 
            representation for the explicitly named nested layouts while preserving the Plan's 
            normative external fields, round-trip laws, identity/closure/order, unknown-member 
            rejection, diagnostics, compatibility exclusions, and structural bounds. Ordered work: 
            (1) survey the accepted P1 codec/evidence and P3 resource/transaction/stream facts; (2) 
            specify nested layout and proof vectors; (3) reconcile the Spec with 
            InspectionAndArtifacts.O4/V4 without inventing public types or a new grammar. Permitted 
            paths: specs/artifact/ArtifactWire.spec and any required spec.index update produced by 
            the Workflow CLI. Shared-write boundary: no implementation/schema code and no Q2 public 
            call-form decision. This is a local prerequisite for T410, not a gate for settled P4/P5 
            tasks.
        acceptance
            Positive: module Spec defines the private nested representation and positive/negative 
            vectors for behavior metadata, turn/lifecycle records, checkpoints, failures/cleanup, 
            resource/transaction/stream facts, context/store/timer/issue facts, and CLI 
            result/error nested data where applicable. Check: workflow check and code-spec review; 
            expected: references resolve and one decoder/encoder ownership is explicit.

            Failure: Spec rejects unknown members and invalid identity/order/correlation, preserves 
            every explicitly required field and bound, and gives diagnostics before Runtime 
            acquisition. Check: Spec verification clauses and workflow check; expected: T410 can 
            implement one closed schema without resolving a public Question.

            Constraint: no public schema types, alternate decoder/migration envelope, or claim of 
            passed runtime behavior is introduced. Check: review of the Spec and route 
            declarations; expected: private design remains replaceable and product contracts remain 
            unchanged.

    T414
        title        StreamProjectionHydration
        status       draft
        priority     medium
        blocked_by   [
                     @T401,
                     @T402,
                     @T410,
                     @task.Rewrite.T311,
                     @task.Rewrite.T312,
                     @task.Rewrite.T317
                     ]
        derives_from [
                     @plan.Streams.O3,
                     @plan.Streams.V3,
                     @plan.Streams.Q1,
                     @plan.PersistenceV2.O4,
                     @plan.PersistenceV2.V4
                     ]
        satisfies    [@plan.Streams.O3, @plan.PersistenceV2.O4]
        description
            After Streams.Q1 is decided, persist only the accepted stream projection and restore it 
            as inert data without serializing or resuming a running stream. Ordered work: (1) 
            consume the approved stream declaration and projection model; (2) include a bounded 
            stream projection in capture/schema; (3) hydrate a fresh session only through its 
            approved lifecycle boundary; (4) prove no adapter invocation occurs during restore. 
            Permitted paths: persistence/hydration.ts, stream projection codec, 
            persistence/test/hydration.test.ts, operation/test/stream-hydration.test.ts. 
            Shared-write boundary: T404 owns resource/transaction hydration; T414 adds only stream 
            projection lanes. This remains draft and does not block T404.
        acceptance
            Positive: accepted stream projection is persisted and restored as inert state; any 
            fresh session begins only after ordinary Runtime readiness and actor ownership. Check: 
            operation/test/stream-hydration.test.ts; expected: projection matches and session 
            generation is fresh.

            Failure: restored bytes never resume or invoke the prior adapter; malformed or 
            unapproved projection is rejected before installation. Check: stream-hydration and 
            persistence hydration tests; expected: adapter invocation count remains zero.

    T415
        title        Stage4PersistenceEvidenceIntegrationGate
        status       open
        priority     high
        blocked_by   [@T401, @T402, @T403, @T404, @T405, @T408, @T409, @T410, @T411, @T412]
        derives_from [
                     @plan.ProjectDelivery.O3,
                     @plan.ProjectDelivery.O4,
                     @plan.PersistenceV2.O1,
                     @plan.PersistenceV2.O2,
                     @plan.PersistenceV2.O3,
                     @plan.PersistenceV2.O4,
                     @plan.PersistenceV2.O5,
                     @plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.O2,
                     @plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.O3,
                     @plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.O4,
                     @plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.V2,
                     @plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.V3,
                     @plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.V4
                     ]
        satisfies    [
                     @plan.ProjectDelivery.O3,
                     @plan.PersistenceV2.O1,
                     @plan.PersistenceV2.O2,
                     @plan.PersistenceV2.O3,
                     @plan.PersistenceV2.O4,
                     @plan.PersistenceV2.O5,
                     @plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.O3,
                     @plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.O4
                     ]
        description
            Prove the settled P4 exit criteria across the single production Runtime, from provider 
            selection through consistent capture, restore/write behavior, evidence acceptance, and 
            bounded artifacts. This is an integration result with cross-owner proof, not a generic 
            test layer. Ordered work: (1) construct the production Runtime inertly and select a 
            compatible durable record at ready; (2) perform a resource/transaction commit through 
            T313 and capture one actor/store/evidence cut; (3) restore resource/transaction facts 
            without replay and verify local interrupted versus remote unknown/reconcile-required 
            truth; (4) issue ordered persistence writes including a failed write retaining the last 
            good record; (5) export/import bounded canonical evidence/artifact and prove 
            bounds/round trip. Permitted paths: persistence/test/stage4-integration.test.ts and a 
            narrow production Runtime wiring fix required for this vertical path. Shared-write 
            boundary: one integrator owns this test; T407/Q2 call forms, T414/Streams.Q1 projection 
            hydration, Resources.Q1 authoring/freshness clauses, and Q1 context-wave-specific 
            capture clauses are explicitly deferred. Do not block independent P5 tasks on these 
            deferrals. Evidence: stage4-integration.test.ts plus the focused owner tests named by 
            T401-T412.
        acceptance
            Positive: one production-owner scenario proves inert construction, detached durable 
            selection/readiness, one committed actor/store/evidence cut, consistent capture, 
            no-replay resource/transaction hydration, ordered writes, and bounded canonical 
            artifact round trip. Check: persistence/test/stage4-integration.test.ts; expected: 
            captured/restored facts match the committed sequence and accepted artifact bytes 
            round-trip within declared bounds.

            Failure: invalid durable identity rejects before acquisition/activation; a capture 
            racing commit is wholly prior or next; restored lookup/transaction/remote work never 
            replays; a failed write preserves last good bytes; over-bound evidence rejects before 
            mutation. Check: stage4-integration.test.ts; expected: each failure preserves the last 
            committed/durable state and emits its owning diagnostic.

            Explicit deferrals: InspectionAndArtifacts.Q2 final call forms (T407); Streams.Q1 
            durable projection/adapter forms (T414); Resources.Q1 authoring, metadata, and 
            freshness lanes (T302/T314/T318); P2 T205 causal-context-specific capture. They are 
            reported as deferred and do not block this settled integration gate or unrelated P5 
            work.

            Explicit decision-task deferrals: Resources.Q1=T315, Transactions.Q2=T316, 
            Streams.Q1=T317, and InspectionAndArtifacts.Q2=T416. T415 does not wait on or implement 
            those local choices; dependent slices remain draft.

